    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.17">
      <p>For the function $$f(x) = 3x^{2} + 2x - 15,$$ find ⓐ $$f(3)$$ ⓑ $$f(-5)$$ ⓒ $$f(0).$$</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.18">
      <p>For the function $$g(x) = 5x^{2} - x - 4,$$ find ⓐ $$g(-2)$$ ⓑ $$g(-1)$$ ⓒ $$g(0).$$</p>
    </note>
    <p>The polynomial functions similar to the one in the next example are used in many fields to determine the height of an object at some time after it is projected into the air. The polynomial in the next function is used specifically for dropping something from 250 ft.</p>
    <example number="5.10">
      <problem>
        <p>The polynomial function $$h(t) = -16t^{2} + 250$$ gives the height of a ball t seconds after it is dropped from a 250-foot tall building. Find the height after $$t = 2$$ seconds.</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <table summary="This table illustrates the step-by-step calculation of the height of an object at t=2 seconds using the function h(t) = -16t^2 + 250, resulting in a height of 186 feet.">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>$$h(t) = -16t^{2} + 250$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>To find $$h(2),$$ substitute $$t = 2.$$</cell>
              <cell>$$h(2) = -16{(2)}^{2} + 250$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$h(2) = -16 \cdot 4 + 250$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$h(2) = -64 + 250$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Simplify.</cell>
              <cell>$$h(2) = 186$$</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell />
              <cell>After 2 seconds the height of the ball is 186 feet.</cell>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </solution>
    </example>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.19">
      <p>The polynomial function $$h(t) = -16t^{2} + 150$$ gives the height of a stone t seconds after it is dropped from a 150-foot tall cliff. Find the height after $$t = 0$$ seconds (the initial height of the object).</p>
    </note>
    <note type="Try It" number="5.20">
      <p>The polynomial function $$h(t) = -16t^{2} + 175$$ gives the height of a ball t seconds after it is dropped from a 175-foot tall bridge. Find the height after $$t = 3$$ seconds.</p>
