  <subsection title="Add and Subtract Polynomial Functions">
    <p>Just as polynomials can be added and subtracted, polynomial functions can also be added and subtracted.</p>
    <note type="Addition and Subtraction of Polynomial Functions">
      <p>For functions $$f(x)$$ and $$g(x),$$</p>
      <equation>$$\begin{array}{l} {\left( {f + g} \right)(x) = f(x) + g(x)} \\ {\left( {f - g} \right)(x) = f(x) - g(x)} \end{array}$$</equation>
    </note>
    <example number="5.11">
      <problem>
        <p>For functions $$f(x) = 3x^{2} - 5x + 7$$ and $$g(x) = x^{2} - 4x - 3,$$ find:</p>
        <p>ⓐ $$\left( {f + g} \right)(x)$$ ⓑ $$\left( {f + g} \right)(3)$$ ⓒ $$\left( {f - g} \right)(x)$$ ⓓ $$\left( {f - g} \right)(-2).$$</p>
      </problem>
