    <instruction>Add and Subtract Polynomial Functions In each example, find ⓐ (f + g)(x) ⓑ (f + g)(2) ⓒ (f − g)(x) ⓓ (f − g)(−3).</instruction>
    <exercise number="73" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <p>$$f(x) = 2x^{2} - 4x + 1$$ and $$g(x) = 5x^{2} + 8x + 3$$</p>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <p>ⓐ $$(f + g)(x) = 7x^{2} + 4x + 4$$ ⓑ $$(f + g)(2) = 40$$ⓒ $$(f - g)(x) = -3x^{2} - 12x - 2$$ⓓ $$(f - g)(-3) = 7$$</p>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
